## Codebase Discoveries
loadPlan centralizes format and effective identity calculation. Single-file identity remains the basename; directory identity comes from ID, and basename remains the physical plan filename. Both metadata and managed directory paths index the same plan. Status, links, parent changes, and progress logs continue through editPlanFile, preserving permissions, unrelated YAML, bodies, and line endings.

Within the canonical OpenSpec subtree, only changes/<change>/plan.md and changes/archive/<archived-change>/plan.md are tracking files. Missing or malformed IDs there remain check findings. Generic plan.md files without ID remain legacy plans. Malformed generic mappings with ID, including duplicate keys in flow mappings, still exclude sibling artifacts. A managed plan at the configured root also excludes its artifacts.

OpenSpec new change creates the directory and .openspec.yaml, not the proposal, design, specifications, or task content. OpenSpec init creates archive and specification directories, including hidden keep files, without requiring a Git repository at the external store root. The init command with --tools none adds no agent integrations. The implementation checks the root selected by openspec list --json before running new change, and it checks the returned change path before writing plan.md. Archive location never implies implementation completion. No Go dependencies changed.

